const repairNotes: Record<string, string[]> = {
  'filipino-customer-onboarding-implementation-coordinator': [
    'A practical onboarding packet should name the customer outcome in the customer\'s own terms, then list the setup artifact that supports each step. For example, an approved user list, field map, test account, or training note can be checked without assuming that the item is technically ready. When a dependency belongs to the customer, show its owner and requested date. When it belongs to delivery, show the internal owner. This makes a Filipino coordinator useful across the handoff without turning a tracker into a promise.',
    'Implementation queues become noisy when every conversation is treated as a task. Separate an action, a question, a decision, and a dependency. An action has an owner and finish evidence. A question needs an answer from a named person. A decision changes scope, configuration, or responsibility. A dependency waits on another record. This distinction gives the customer owner a short review list and prevents routine follow-up from being mistaken for authorization.',
    'Use a readiness review that follows the customer journey: intake, access, configuration input, test evidence, training material, and handoff. At each stage, record what was checked, what was not checked, and what would make the item ready. A coordinator may compare a submitted field against an approved requirement, but should not decide that an ambiguous field is acceptable. That stop rule protects both the customer record and the implementation team.',
    'A useful exception note is specific enough for someone outside the original conversation to act. It can say that the account identifier differs between the intake form and the approved system, attach both source references, and ask which value controls. It should not say merely “customer issue.” Preserve the original values, the time checked, and the owner response. The history matters when a later configuration question depends on an earlier correction.',
    'Review the first implementation cycle with the customer owner and delivery owner together. Ask whether every queue item had one source, one owner, and one finish condition. Look for hidden decisions such as an unapproved integration, an assumed data mapping, or a timeline inferred from a meeting invitation. Those findings should narrow the role brief or improve the example set before the queue grows.',
    'For Philippine working hours and client overlap, keep the handoff record more authoritative than informal chat. The record should show the last confirmed state, the next action, and the person who can answer an open question. A substitute coordinator can then continue the evidence trail without recreating private messages or guessing whether silence means approval. Continuity is a control on the work, not a reason to broaden access.',
  ],
  'filipino-revenue-operations-forecast-support-coordinator': [
    'A forecast support packet should begin with a frozen reporting cut: the date, timezone, pipeline view, filters, and export identifier. Record the field definitions for amount, stage, expected close, and owner rather than assuming each system uses the same meaning. A Filipino coordinator can assemble and reconcile these inputs, then return a precise exception. The sales leader retains the judgment about confidence, timing, and what belongs in a committed view.',
    'Separate a pipeline fact from a forecast assertion. A dated meeting, proposal status, or customer note is an observed record. “Likely to close” is an interpretation that requires sales authority and context. Keep those statements in different fields and use the source timestamp for both. This prevents a prepared spreadsheet from quietly becoming a commercial commitment when it is copied into a review meeting.',
    'Use a reconciliation table with one row per exception: record identifier, source A, source B, difference, last checked time, reason code, and owner question. Useful reason codes include duplicate opportunity, stale activity, missing next step, conflicting amount, and stage confirmation needed. The coordinator should preserve the disagreement rather than select a value that makes the total appear more coherent.',
    'A weekly review can sample an ordinary opportunity, an opportunity with no recent activity, and one whose amount differs between sources. For each sample, verify the filter, source row, reporting period, calculation, and handoff. If a correction changes a manager\'s interpretation, document it as an owner decision. Do not backfill history to make a prior forecast look consistent.',
    'Forecast operations often cross sales, finance, and customer success. Name which team owns each field and which team may answer an exception. A coordinator may request a missing confirmation and schedule the review, but should not change a stage, discount, close date, or customer-facing statement because a meeting is approaching. Commercial authority must remain visible at the field level.',
    'Measure the support lane through checked records, open exceptions by cause, time awaiting owner confirmation, duplicate candidates, and reviewer corrections. These measures describe the quality of preparation. They do not establish revenue, conversion, forecast accuracy, or future performance. Expand only when the source hierarchy, access list, reporting cut, and escalation owner can be explained without relying on personal memory.',
  ],
  'filipino-hr-policy-documentation-coordinator': [
    'A policy register should connect the employee-facing document to its approved source and decision history. Record the policy owner, version, effective date, audience, approval state, publication location, and next review. A coordinator can check whether the published copy matches the approved version. They cannot decide that an unsigned draft applies simply because it appears in a shared folder.',
    'Acknowledgment tracking needs careful status vocabulary. Sent, delivered, opened, acknowledged, returned, and exception are different observations. None should be converted into agreement, understanding, or legal compliance without an authorized interpretation. Keep the version attached to every status so a later reminder does not accidentally ask an employee to acknowledge an obsolete document.',
    'Employee questions should travel with the smallest necessary amount of personal information. Capture the policy section, neutral question, document version, and requested decision. Keep medical, disciplinary, compensation, and identity details in the approved HR system. A coordinator can route the question across Philippine and client working hours while HR decides what the policy means in the individual situation.',
    'Use a private exception queue for missing approvals, conflicting versions, inaccessible documents, and questions that may affect employment. Each item needs an owner, due point, access rule, and next action. Avoid a generic pending status because it exposes too little to the reviewer and encourages someone to answer from memory. Preserve the source files and the prior decision record.',
    'A review sample should include a clean delivery, a delivery tied to the wrong version, and an employee question awaiting interpretation. Check recipient, source, date, access, and route. Record whether the correction was a transcription error, a distribution problem, or an HR decision. Only the policy owner may approve a wording or scope change.',
    'A Filipino documentation coordinator can support recurring policy administration without becoming an HR decision-maker. Define the systems, named account, minimum fields, reviewer, confidentiality boundary, and removal step before access is granted. Measure documents inventoried, version conflicts, acknowledgments by state, unanswered questions, and corrections. Those are workflow signals, not conclusions about employee conduct or policy effectiveness.',
  ],
  'filipino-ecommerce-refund-case-preparation-coordinator': [
    'A refund case packet should establish one event timeline from order creation through fulfillment, delivery, customer contact, return activity, and payment status. Keep each event linked to its source and timestamp. The coordinator may assemble the chronology and identify a missing scan or message; the authorized reviewer decides whether the evidence meets policy and what remedy, if any, is appropriate.',
    'Different case types require different evidence. A damaged item may need a customer image and carrier note. A duplicate charge may need payment references. A missing parcel may need fulfillment and delivery events. A late order may require the promised window and actual scan. The checklist should identify these differences without turning a reason code into an automatic refund decision.',
    'Keep customer language intact when it carries a claim or requested remedy. Add a neutral coordinator note that distinguishes reported, observed, and unresolved information. Do not describe a customer as fraudulent, entitled, or ineligible unless an authorized system and reviewer provide that determination. This protects the case record while making the next handoff easier to understand.',
    'Before opening work, search approved identifiers for an existing case and link related contacts. If duplicates exist, preserve both histories and identify the record that owns the next action. A case should state what evidence is present, what is missing, who is waiting, and when it was last checked. “Pending” alone creates repeat requests and can cause inconsistent customer treatment.',
    'A quality sample should compare a routine request, an incomplete request, and a request with conflicting order and customer records. Verify policy version, source links, timestamps, access, and escalation. Corrections should name whether the problem was intake, transcription, duplicate handling, or a remedy decision. Never delete inconvenient evidence to shorten the queue.',
    'For Filipino ecommerce support operations, the safe boundary is preparation: gather, label, link, and route. Keep refund authorization, fraud review, payment changes, account access, and customer promises with the named owner. Track evidence gaps, duplicate links, owner waits, policy questions, and reviewer corrections. These measures describe case readiness, not refund speed, fraud detection, or customer satisfaction.',
  ],
  'filipino-website-analytics-reporting-coordinator': [
    'A reporting request should identify the business question before it identifies a chart. Record property, page set, date range, timezone, attribution setting, filters, audience, and intended reader. A coordinator can reproduce an approved view and document its settings. The site owner decides whether the question is useful and how the result should influence content or operating choices.',
    'Metric names are not definitions. A page view, session, user, event, and conversion can change meaning with filters and collection rules. Put the definition beside the value and preserve the raw export or approved dashboard link. If the same period produces different values in two views, report the difference and route the measurement question instead of selecting the more favorable number.',
    'Website reporting for FilipinoOutsource.com should keep page identity visible. Include the route, title, content group, extraction time, and any redirect or duplicate-path note. Do not merge paths merely because their titles look similar. A route change can explain a reporting difference, and that explanation belongs in the review record rather than being hidden by a cleanup formula.',
    'Separate observation from interpretation in the report layout. “The approved view shows fewer sessions in the period” is a measured statement. “The article underperformed because the introduction was weak” is an analysis that needs an owner and evidence. Labels such as observed, definition-dependent, and owner interpretation help a reviewer see where the coordination work ends.',
    'Use three test cases for every new report: the normal view, a deliberately filtered view, and a source mismatch. A second reviewer should reproduce the value from the documented settings. Corrections should identify filter, timezone, source, calculation, transcription, or interpretation. This is especially important when reports are prepared across Philippine and client time zones.',
    'A bounded analytics lane can measure reports delivered, missing definitions, source mismatches, returned summaries, and review corrections. It must not claim traffic growth, ranking, conversion performance, or a causal marketing result from those process signals. Confirm approved fields, privacy limits, report audience, and decision owner before adding another dashboard or data source.',
  ],
  'filipino-vendor-compliance-records-coordinator': [
    'A supplier evidence register should distinguish document presence from document acceptance. Record supplier identifier, document family, issuing source, received date, version, expiry or review date, checklist state, and responsible reviewer. The coordinator can verify that a file is present and legible against instructions. Procurement or compliance decides whether it is valid, sufficient, or acceptable.',
    'Document exceptions need observable language. Missing, unreadable, expired, conflicting, and owner review required are useful states. “Noncompliant” may be a determination outside the role. Preserve the submitted file, source reference, and receipt time when a problem is found. Do not edit a supplier document or replace an uncertain record simply to clear the queue.',
    'Renewal reminders should include the controlling source date, supplier owner, next action, and review destination. An approaching date is a reason to request review, not proof that a supplier has lost or retained approval. When dates conflict, display both values and ask which record governs. Never choose the later date to make the queue appear current.',
    'Sensitive supplier material requires a narrow access design. Tax, banking, insurance, identity, and legal files should stay in the approved system with named access and a review date. The coordinator needs only the fields required for routing. Convenience exports and personal folders create a second record that the compliance owner may not be able to control.',
    'Sample a complete record, an expired record, and a conflict between two supplier documents. Check identifier, source, version, access, date, and owner route. Classify corrections as intake, transcription, version, source, or decision. A dated log lets procurement see recurring evidence problems without turning them into unsupported claims about a vendor.',
    'For a Filipino vendor records lane, define the checklist, source hierarchy, reviewer, escalation path, and confidentiality rule before adding volume. Track records received, missing evidence, upcoming reviews, owner decisions, access exceptions, and corrections. These signals show queue condition; they do not establish legal compliance, supplier risk, or approval. Expand only after the decision boundary is explicit.',
  ],
  'filipino-product-support-release-notes-coordinator': [
    'A release-notes packet should begin with the approved change record, product area, release state, intended audience, owner, and source version. Compare each public sentence with the approved description. A coordinator can identify an omission or mismatch, but cannot add a capability, customer benefit, availability statement, or release date that the source does not establish.',
    'Support readers need distinctions between confirmed behavior, known limitation, migration note, and unresolved question. Keep those labels visible. A draft that says “available soon” is not a confirmed date, and a ticket that says “planned” is not a shipped feature. Route ambiguous language to the product owner before it reaches a support channel.',
    'Organize notes around the questions a support team can answer: what changed, which users may encounter it, what approved guidance applies, what evidence to request, and where an exception goes. Keep implementation detail out of public copy unless it has been approved for that audience. The role prepares clarity; the product owner controls the claim.',
    'Use a channel matrix for internal support notes, customer-facing notes, help-center content, and account-specific messages. Each channel can have a different reviewer and effective date. Do not reuse a sentence across channels just because it is concise. Customer commitments, rollout timing, and limitation wording need an owner decision in the destination channel.',
    'Review one ordinary change, one change with a limitation, and one change whose date or behavior is unresolved. Verify ticket, specification, approval, version, audience, and publication status. Record whether the correction concerned source mismatch, unsupported wording, missing limitation, or release judgment. Preserve the prior approved note when history matters.',
    'A Filipino product support coordinator can maintain an evidence-backed release queue while product and support leaders retain authority. Measure packets checked, missing approvals, source mismatches, returned notes, unresolved dates, and reviewer corrections. These measures do not prove adoption, reliability, customer value, or release success. Expand only after channel ownership and stop rules are documented.',
  ],
  'filipino-insurance-claims-intake-coordinator': [
    'Claims intake should establish a neutral file spine: claim reference, reported event, policy reference, received documents, chronology, contact record, and missing evidence. Keep each item linked to its source and receipt time. A coordinator can make the file reviewable and ask for a missing document; an authorized claims reviewer decides coverage, liability, severity, and settlement.',
    'Use reported, documented, verified, disputed, and awaiting review as separate states. A customer statement is important evidence but not a finding. A document can be present without proving the point it is offered to support. This vocabulary helps a Filipino intake coordinator preserve the claimant’s account without making an insurance determination.',
    'Different claim types need different checklists. Property damage may involve photos, estimates, and incident details. A health-related file may require tighter handling and a defined clinical or claims owner. A motor claim may involve a report, vehicle details, and repair evidence. The coordinator follows the approved intake rule and stops when the rule does not cover the case.',
    'Escalations should state the exact question, relevant policy version, evidence attached, conflicting information, and decision owner. Avoid shorthand such as “looks covered” or “probably valid.” Keep sensitive records in approved systems, minimize copied personal data, and do not disclose internal review rules to a claimant without authorization.',
    'Sample a complete intake, an intake with missing evidence, and a file with inconsistent dates or identities. Check source, chronology, access, status, and route. Corrections should distinguish transcription, duplicate, source conflict, and claims judgment. Preserve the original submission and the coordinator’s dated observation so later review does not depend on memory.',
    'Measure documents received, missing items, duplicate links, owner waits, privacy escalations, and reviewer corrections. These are intake signals, not claim outcomes, settlement speed, coverage conclusions, or fraud findings. Define the permitted systems, named reviewer, emergency path, and stop rules before expanding the lane for Philippines-based operations support.',
  ],
  'filipino-community-moderation-queue-coordinator': [
    'A moderation queue should preserve reported content, report time, rule reference, context needed for review, current status, and authorized reviewer. A coordinator can organize evidence and identify duplicates. They should not decide removal, suspension, safety response, or appeal outcome unless the role has an explicit rule and delegated authority for that exact action.',
    'Context matters: a post, reply, image, account history, and report reason may each be relevant, but collect only what the approved workflow permits. Keep the reporter and subject identities narrow. If the content may indicate immediate safety risk, use the named escalation path and preserve the evidence rather than improvising a response.',
    'Rule references should be precise enough for a reviewer to inspect. Avoid turning a vague label such as “bad content” into an enforcement conclusion. When more than one rule may apply, record both and ask which review path governs. The coordinator makes ambiguity visible; the moderation owner interprets the rule and chooses the action.',
    'A queue needs separate states for new report, duplicate, awaiting context, reviewer decision, appeal review, and closed. The state should show who owns the next step and what evidence is missing. Do not close a report because it is old, because a similar item was closed, or because a message was sent without an authorized decision.',
    'Sample a routine report, an ambiguous report, and a report with a safety escalation. Check content reference, rule version, privacy, timestamps, and reviewer route. Corrections should identify evidence capture, duplicate handling, classification, or enforcement judgment. Preserve the record required for an appeal without retaining unnecessary personal details.',
    'For a Filipino moderation support lane, measure reports received, duplicate links, context gaps, owner waits, escalation states, and reviewer corrections. These measures do not prove platform safety, fairness, response speed, or enforcement quality. Confirm the rule set, access, emergency path, and appeal owner before adding another content category.',
  ],
  'filipino-learning-content-qa-coordinator': [
    'A learning-content QA packet should identify course, lesson, version, audience, learning objective, source material, reviewer, and status. The coordinator can check completeness and link integrity against an approved checklist. They should not change instructional meaning, certify correctness in a specialist subject, or infer that a complete file produces a learning outcome.',
    'Check the content in layers: required sections, labels, links, media, accessibility fields, source references, and assessment instructions. Record the exact location of a problem and the expected evidence for correction. “Needs work” is weaker than “the answer key references version two while the lesson displays version one.”',
    'Keep content QA separate from grading and learner decisions. A missing rubric field is a QA finding; whether a learner passes is an educator decision. If a question has more than one defensible answer or a source is unclear, preserve it as an educator review item rather than silently selecting a preferred response.',
    'Use version control for lesson files, answer keys, translations, captions, and downloadable material. A reviewer should know which package was checked and which package is intended for release. Do not replace the source file while fixing formatting. Store the correction request and owner response with the version that prompted it.',
    'Sample a complete lesson, a lesson with a broken dependency, and an item that needs subject-matter review. Verify source, links, labels, access, version, and destination. Classify corrections as missing asset, formatting, source mismatch, accessibility check, or educator decision. This keeps the queue teachable for a Philippines-based support team.',
    'Measure lessons checked, missing assets, broken links, source questions, returned packages, and reviewer corrections. These signals describe content preparation, not instructional quality, learner completion, grades, or educational results. Expand only when an educator has confirmed the checklist, subject boundaries, access rules, and release owner.',
  ],
  'filipino-business-continuity-records-coordinator': [
    'A continuity record should identify the business dependency, service or process, owner, alternate contact, source date, review date, and access classification. The coordinator can maintain the register and flag stale information. Leadership decides priority, acceptable risk, recovery order, and whether a dependency is sufficiently resilient.',
    'Contact records need more than a name. Keep last confirmation, channel, time zone, alternate path, and the source of each value. An old number is not proof of coverage. If a contact cannot be confirmed, show the dependency and route it. Do not copy sensitive personal details into a broad continuity document merely to make it look complete.',
    'Exercise notes should distinguish the approved scenario from what actually occurred. Capture date, participants, observed actions, unavailable dependencies, unresolved questions, and follow-up owner. An exercise can reveal a gap without proving how a real incident will unfold. Keep assumptions and limitations beside the observation so a later reviewer does not overread the result.',
    'For systems and suppliers, record the evidence that supports a dependency claim: current owner, approved contact, service reference, manual fallback, or exercise action. Do not invent a fallback because a plan template has a blank field. A missing fallback is a leadership decision, and the record should make that decision visible.',
    'Sample an ordinary dependency, an expired contact, and an exercise action awaiting ownership. Check source, date, access, next action, and escalation. Corrections should distinguish stale data, missing ownership, source conflict, and risk acceptance. Preserve the dated decision record so a later team can tell what was known at the time.',
    'A Filipino continuity records lane can support disciplined preparation without promising recovery time or resilience. Measure dependencies inventoried, confirmations pending, overdue reviews, exercise actions, access exceptions, and owner decisions. These are evidence signals, not guarantees. Confirm confidentiality, emergency routing, named leadership owner, and risk boundary before expanding the register.',
  ],
};

const depthExtensions: Record<string, string[]> = {
  'filipino-customer-onboarding-implementation-coordinator': ['On a real implementation queue, the most useful handoff is not a percentage complete. It is a compact decision packet that lets the customer owner answer one question at a time. Start with the agreed outcome, then show the inputs received, the inputs still missing, the dependency owner, the evidence checked, and the next review point. If an account list contains a value that does not match the approved field map, quote the field names and preserve both source references. If a test result is unavailable, say what test was expected and who can provide it. This keeps the Filipino coordinator focused on preparation while giving a delivery owner enough context to act. The packet should also record whether a request is ordinary implementation work or a scope change. A request to add a new system, import a new data class, change an access level, or move a committed date is not just another checklist item. It needs an explicit decision and should remain visibly blocked until that decision exists. A short weekly sample can compare an item that moved smoothly with one that stopped. Reviewers should ask whether the source was approved, whether the completion evidence was observable, and whether any promise was inferred from silence. Those questions improve the routine without granting the coordinator configuration authority.'] ,
  'filipino-revenue-operations-forecast-support-coordinator': ['Forecast support is strongest when the review packet makes uncertainty easy to locate. Freeze the source view before summarizing it, then preserve the export identifier, filter settings, field definitions, and extraction time. A Filipino coordinator can reconcile record identifiers and point out that an amount, stage, or expected-close field differs between systems. The packet should never hide that difference behind a single total. For each exception, state the observable facts, the source that supplied each fact, the date checked, and the sales owner who must decide. A stale activity record may require a seller update; a conflicting amount may require a manager decision; a missing close date may require a conversation rather than a guessed value. These are different queues and should not share one vague status. Separate operational measures from commercial conclusions as well. Records checked, exceptions returned, time awaiting owner confirmation, and duplicate candidates describe the preparation lane. They do not establish forecast accuracy, expected revenue, or the likelihood of a deal. A useful review samples a normal record, a record with incomplete activity, and a record where two approved sources disagree. The reviewer traces each value back to its source and asks whether the coordinator stopped at the right boundary. If a recurring exception is resolved, document the rule and effective date only after sales leadership approves it.'] ,
  'filipino-hr-policy-documentation-coordinator': ['Policy documentation requires version discipline because a small administrative error can give an employee the wrong reference. Keep the approved source, published copy, distribution audience, effective date, and acknowledgment record connected. When a revised policy is issued, record which version was sent to which audience and whether an earlier acknowledgment remains valid under the owner’s instruction. The Filipino coordinator can identify a mismatch, resend an approved document, or prepare a list of unanswered questions. They should not tell an employee how a policy applies to a personal circumstance. An escalation should contain the smallest necessary context, the relevant section, the exact question, and the authorized reviewer. Separate ordinary publication work from matters involving compensation, discipline, medical information, protected leave, or an employment consequence. Those cases belong in the approved confidential path, not in a broad tracking sheet. A practical quality review checks three records: a correct acknowledgment, a missing acknowledgment, and a question attached to an outdated version. The reviewer confirms recipient, version, timestamp, permission, and next owner action. Measure the states of the workflow rather than claiming that employees understood or agreed. If managers repeatedly ask the same interpretive question, improve the source guidance through the policy owner; do not let a coordinator’s informal answer become an unapproved policy amendment.'] ,
  'filipino-ecommerce-refund-case-preparation-coordinator': ['Refund preparation should make the reviewer’s next decision easier without deciding it in advance. Build a chronology from order creation, payment authorization, fulfillment, delivery, customer contact, return activity, and any prior case. Keep event times, identifiers, source links, and the customer’s original wording. A Filipino coordinator can notice that a delivery scan is missing or that two contacts refer to the same order; the coordinator cannot decide whether a remedy is owed. Use different evidence checklists for damage, non-delivery, duplicate charge, late arrival, and unauthorized transaction questions. A checklist tells the owner what is present and what remains uncertain. It must not act as an automatic approval rule. Keep reported, observed, and unresolved information in separate fields. Avoid labels that imply fraud, entitlement, or ineligibility unless an authorized system and reviewer have supplied that decision. Before requesting another document, check for duplicate cases and link related records so the customer is not asked twice for the same evidence. A sample review should test a routine case, an incomplete case, and a case with conflicting identifiers. Confirm the policy version, source timestamps, privacy handling, and escalation route. Process measures such as evidence gaps, duplicate links, owner waits, and correction causes describe readiness only. They do not promise refund speed or customer satisfaction.'] ,
  'filipino-website-analytics-reporting-coordinator': ['A website analytics packet should be reproducible by someone who did not build it. Begin with the question, property, route set, date range, timezone, filters, attribution setting, and intended reader. Preserve the approved view or raw export alongside the formatted report. A Filipino coordinator may record that a page path has a particular value under those settings, but should not convert that observation into a cause, recommendation, or performance claim. Keep route identity visible for FilipinoOutsource.com content. Redirects, duplicate paths, renamed pages, and tracking changes can alter a number without changing the underlying work, so they belong in the exception notes. Use separate labels for observed, definition-dependent, and owner interpretation. A report that says a count changed is different from an analysis that says why it changed. Test each new report with a normal view, a deliberately filtered view, and a mismatch between two approved sources. The second reviewer should be able to reproduce the value from the documented settings and identify any calculation or timezone difference. Confirm privacy limits and audience before exporting fields that could identify individuals. Track reports delivered, missing definitions, source mismatches, returned summaries, and corrections. Those are workflow measures; they are not evidence of traffic growth, rankings, conversions, or causal marketing impact.'] ,
  'filipino-vendor-compliance-records-coordinator': ['Supplier records become safer when the queue distinguishes evidence handling from compliance judgment. For each supplier, record the document family, identifier, issuing source, received date, version, review or expiry date, checklist result, access class, and named reviewer. A file being present does not prove that it is authentic, sufficient, current, or accepted. The Filipino coordinator can check presence and legibility against an approved instruction, then route anything that needs interpretation. Use observable reason codes such as missing, unreadable, expired, conflicting, or owner review required. Do not rewrite “owner review required” as “noncompliant” merely to make a dashboard simpler. Renewal reminders should show the source date and action owner; an approaching date is not a decision about vendor approval. If two records carry different dates, retain both and ask which source governs. Keep tax, banking, insurance, identity, and legal material in the approved system with minimum necessary access. A quality sample should include a complete file, an expired file, and a source conflict. Check the identifier, version, permission, date, and route, then classify any correction. Measures such as received files, missing evidence, upcoming reviews, access exceptions, and owner decisions describe queue condition. They do not establish legal compliance, supplier risk, or procurement approval.'] ,
  'filipino-product-support-release-notes-coordinator': ['Release-notes coordination is a source comparison task before it is a writing task. Start from the approved change record and keep the product area, release state, intended audience, owner, and source version beside the draft. Compare every sentence with the approved material. A Filipino coordinator can flag an omission, unclear limitation, or unsupported phrase, but cannot add a capability, availability statement, customer benefit, or date. Support readers need to know whether a behavior is confirmed, limited, planned, or unresolved. Keep those states separate so “planned” does not become “shipped” when a note is shortened. Build a channel matrix for internal support guidance, customer-facing notes, help-center copy, and account-specific messages. Different audiences may need different reviewers and effective dates; a concise sentence is not automatically reusable across all channels. Review one ordinary change, one change with a limitation, and one with an unresolved date. Trace each to its ticket or specification and record whether a correction concerns source mismatch, missing limitation, unsupported wording, or product judgment. Preserve prior approved notes when history matters. Measure packets checked, missing approvals, returned drafts, unresolved dates, and reviewer corrections. These measures describe preparation and do not establish adoption, reliability, customer value, or release success.'] ,
  'filipino-insurance-claims-intake-coordinator': ['Claims intake should make the file complete without making it conclusive. Establish a neutral spine containing the claim reference, reported event, policy reference, documents received, chronology, contacts, missing evidence, and authorized reviewer. Keep each item tied to its source and receipt time. Use reported, documented, verified, disputed, and awaiting review as separate states. A claimant statement can be important evidence without being a finding, and a document can be present without proving the issue it was submitted to support. Different claim types may require different checklists. Property damage, motor incidents, and health-related records can involve different evidence and tighter access controls. The coordinator follows the approved checklist and stops when a case falls outside it. An escalation should state the exact question, relevant policy version, evidence attached, conflicting details, and decision owner. Avoid shorthand such as “covered” or “valid” unless the authorized reviewer has made that determination. Preserve original submissions and minimize copied personal information. A quality sample should include a complete intake, a missing-document intake, and a file with inconsistent dates or identities. Corrections should distinguish transcription, duplicate handling, source conflict, and claims judgment. Track documents received, missing items, owner waits, privacy escalations, and corrections. Those are intake signals, not coverage, settlement, fraud, or claim-outcome conclusions.'] ,
  'filipino-community-moderation-queue-coordinator': ['A moderation queue should help an authorized reviewer see context without broadening access or making an enforcement decision by accident. Preserve the reported content reference, report time, rule version, report reason, permitted context, current state, and reviewer route. A Filipino coordinator may link duplicates and identify missing context. They should not remove content, suspend an account, assess a safety threat, or decide an appeal unless the exact rule and delegated authority say so. Use separate states for new report, duplicate, awaiting context, reviewer decision, appeal review, and closed. Each state needs a next owner and a reason. A report should not close because it is old, because similar content was previously reviewed, or because a message was sent without a decision. Collect only the context allowed by the workflow and keep reporter and subject identities narrow. If content may indicate immediate danger, follow the named escalation path and preserve the evidence rather than inventing a response. Sample a routine report, an ambiguous report, and one with a safety escalation. Check the rule reference, timestamps, privacy, duplicate handling, and reviewer route. Measure reports received, context gaps, owner waits, escalation states, and corrections. Those measures do not prove safety, fairness, response speed, or enforcement quality.'] ,
  'filipino-learning-content-qa-coordinator': ['Learning-content QA should prove what was checked, not certify what learners will achieve. Record course, lesson, version, audience, objective, source material, reviewer, and status. Check required sections, labels, links, media, accessibility fields, source references, and assessment instructions against an approved checklist. Identify the exact location of a problem and the evidence needed to correct it. A Filipino coordinator can note that an answer key references a different version from the displayed lesson; an educator decides which content is correct. Keep formatting fixes separate from changes to instructional meaning, grading, or subject-matter accuracy. Version control should include lessons, answer keys, translations, captions, and downloads so a reviewer knows exactly which package was checked and which package is intended for release. Sample a complete lesson, one with a broken dependency, and one requiring subject review. Verify source, links, labels, access, version, and destination. Classify corrections as missing asset, formatting, source mismatch, accessibility check, or educator decision. Measure lessons checked, missing assets, broken links, source questions, returned packages, and corrections. These are preparation signals, not claims about learning quality, grades, completion, or educational outcomes.'] ,
  'filipino-customer-feedback-evidence-coordinator': ['Feedback evidence is useful when the owner can inspect how a note became a coded record. Define the question, channels, time window, audience, permissions, and coding rules before organizing responses. Preserve the customer’s wording, source, date, permitted context, and any uncertainty. A Filipino coordinator can apply an approved code or retain multiple codes where the rule permits; the research or customer owner decides what a theme means and whether it should affect prioritization. Keep identifiable information in the approved system and do not export raw responses into a broad working file. Check whether a source permits internal use, quotation, or follow-up; if that permission is unclear, route the question. An evidence packet should state the method, sample boundary, source links, coding notes, exclusions, and open questions. Never imply that a small or filtered set represents every customer. Review a clear response, an ambiguous response, and one with missing permission. Trace each code to the rule and preserve prior decisions when comparisons may matter. Track responses received, permission gaps, uncoded items, code questions, owner reviews, and corrections. These measures describe evidence management, not satisfaction, demand, or product conclusions.'] ,
};

const depthBoosts: Record<string, string[]> = Object.fromEntries(topics.filter((topic) => topic.slug !== 'filipino-customer-onboarding-implementation-coordinator').map((topic) => [topic.slug, ['For ' + topic.lane + ', the first review cycle should be designed around evidence a manager can inspect without asking the worker to reconstruct the work from memory. Begin with a small sample that includes an ordinary item, an incomplete item, and an item that must stop at a consequential boundary. For each item, preserve the approved source, the fields checked, the reason for the current state, the named owner, and the next action. The purpose of the sample is not to produce a flattering score. It is to learn whether the intake rule is clear, whether the finished output is observable, and whether the escalation contains the exact question that the owner must answer. Keep a dated record of corrections and distinguish a missing field from a source conflict, a transcription mistake, and a decision outside the role. If the same question appears repeatedly, revise the written example only after the responsible owner confirms the rule. A coordinator supporting FilipinoOutsource.com can then work consistently across client and Philippine schedules while preserving authority with the business owner. Before adding another system or category, confirm the permission, reviewer, retention expectation, and stop rule. Queue counts and aging help manage the work, but they are not claims about the customer, employee, supplier, learner, claim, community, product, or business outcome represented by the records.']]));

const feedbackDepth: Record<string, string[]> = {
  'filipino-customer-feedback-evidence-coordinator': ['A careful evidence lane also needs a record of how collection conditions affect interpretation. Note whether a response came from a survey, interview, support conversation, or another approved channel; record the invitation or sampling rule when it is available; and keep the collection window beside the source. A coordinator can describe those conditions and flag a gap, but the customer owner decides whether the material answers the original question. Keep direct quotations distinct from coordinator summaries, and mark translations, redactions, truncation, or transcription as changes that a reviewer should know about. If a participant asks not to be contacted again, route that instruction through the approved privacy path rather than placing it in a general notes file. When a response appears to contain a request for support, separate that request from the research record and send it to the appropriate owner. For coding review, compare a clear example, a multi-theme example, and one whose permission or context is incomplete. Ask whether the approved code was applied, whether the source remains inspectable, and whether the record makes uncertainty visible. A manager can then decide whether a theme deserves attention without mistaking a prepared sample for a population claim. Measure the evidence process with source completeness, permission questions, coding disagreements, returned records, and time awaiting review. Keep prioritization, product decisions, sentiment conclusions, and customer-wide claims outside this role. Preserve the original response and the reviewer question whenever a code changes, so a later comparison can distinguish a new theme from a revised classification.'] ,
};

const depthTail: Record<string, string[]> = Object.fromEntries(topics.map((topic) => [topic.slug, ['The review record should also state what the worker was not asked to do. That boundary is part of a useful handoff: it tells the owner that the coordinator did not approve a remedy, interpret a policy, alter a customer commitment, or turn an observed record into a business conclusion. Keep the source link, checking time, owner response, and effective date together when a correction changes the instruction. This small discipline makes the queue teachable, reviewable, and safe to continue across shifts. A manager should be able to open the record later and understand the order of events, the evidence that was available, the evidence that was missing, and the person who had authority to resolve the open question. If the work crosses a time zone or a substitute takes over, the dated handoff should be enough to continue safely without relying on private chat, memory, or an assumption that silence meant approval.']]));

